    {
      "id": "u9",
      "num": 9,
      "level": "A2",
      "title": "The definite object",
      "goal": "Use the accusative, tell definite and indefinite objects apart, and get the word order right.",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "t": "p",
          "text": "The <b>accusative</b> marks the direct object when it is definite (known, specified, already mentioned). It is formed with <b>-(y)ı / -i / -u / -ü</b>. An indefinite object takes no suffix."
        },
        {
          "t": "table",
          "caption": "Forming the accusative",
          "head": [
            "Word",
            "Accusative",
            "Meaning"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "<tur>ev</tur>",
              "<tur>evi</tur>",
              "the house"
            ],
            [
              "<tur>okul</tur>",
              "<tur>okulu</tur>",
              "the school"
            ],
            [
              "<tur>kitap</tur>",
              "<tur>kitabı</tur>",
              "the book"
            ],
            [
              "<tur>masa</tur>",
              "<tur>masayı</tur>",
              "the table"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "t": "note",
          "kind": "tip",
          "tag": "Definite or indefinite?",
          "text": "<tur>Kitabı okudum.</tur> = I read the book (a specific one). <tur>Bir kitap okudum.</tur> = I read a book. The suffix changes the meaning and the speaker's focus."
        },
        {
          "t": "table",
          "caption": "Object pronouns",
          "head": [
            "Subject",
            "Object",
            "Example"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "ben",
              "<tur>beni</tur>",
              "<tur>Beni anlıyor musun?</tur>"
            ],
            [
              "sen",
              "<tur>seni</tur>",
              "<tur>Seni dün gördüm.</tur>"
            ],
            [
              "o",
              "<tur>onu</tur>",
              "<tur>Onu tanıyorum.</tur>"
            ],
            [
              "biz",
              "<tur>bizi</tur>",
              "<tur>Bizi davet ettiler.</tur>"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "t": "ex",
          "items": [
            {
              "tr": "Kitabı okudum.",
              "fr": "I read the book."
            },
            {
              "tr": "Bir kitap okudum.",
              "fr": "I read a book."
            },
            {
              "tr": "Beni anlıyor musun?",
              "fr": "Do you understand me?"
            },
            {
              "tr": "Mehmet'e anahtarı verdim.",
              "fr": "I gave the key to Mehmet."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "t": "note",
          "kind": "info",
          "tag": "Word order",
          "text": "The neutral order is <b>Subject – Object – Verb</b> (SOV). You can move an element to the front to highlight it, but the verb generally stays at the end of the sentence."
        }
      ],
