      "quiz": [
        {
          "q": "How do you say «I saw the house»?",
          "options": [
            "Evi gördüm.",
            "Ev gördüm.",
            "Eve gördüm."
          ],
          "a": 0,
          "why": "The house is a definite object: ev + i = evi, placed before the verb."
        },
        {
          "q": "What is the object pronoun of «ben»?",
          "options": [
            "beni",
            "bana",
            "benim"
          ],
          "a": 0,
          "why": "The accusative of ben is beni; bana is the dative and benim the genitive."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "u10",
      "num": 10,
      "level": "A2",
      "title": "Habits and politeness",
      "goal": "Talk about your habits, make a polite request and refer to repeated actions in the past.",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "t": "p",
          "text": "The <b>present simple</b> (or habitual present) is formed with <b>-ir / -ır / -ur / -ür</b>, or simply <b>-r</b> after a vowel. It describes what repeats, a general truth or a preference."
        },
        {
          "t": "table",
          "caption": "gelmek (to come) in the present simple",
          "head": [
            "Person",
            "Affirmative",
            "Negative"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "ben",
              "<tur>gelirim</tur>",
              "<tur>gelmem</tur>"
            ],
            [
              "sen",
              "<tur>gelirsin</tur>",
              "<tur>gelmezsin</tur>"
            ],
            [
              "o",
              "<tur>gelir</tur>",
              "<tur>gelmez</tur>"
            ],
            [
              "biz",
              "<tur>geliriz</tur>",
              "<tur>gelmeyiz</tur>"
            ],
            [
              "siz",
              "<tur>gelirsiniz</tur>",
              "<tur>gelmezsiniz</tur>"
            ],
            [
              "onlar",
              "<tur>gelirler</tur>",
              "<tur>gelmezler</tur>"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "t": "p",
          "text": "The <b>habitual past</b> adds <b>-erdi / -ardı</b>: <tur>gelirdim</tur> (I used to come, I would come). It is used for repeated memories: <tur>Çocukken her yaz köye giderdik.</tur>"
        },
        {
          "t": "p",
          "text": "For a polite request, use the present simple + <tur>mi</tur>: <tur>Bana yardım eder misiniz?</tur> (Could you help me?), <tur>Bir dakika bekler misiniz?</tur> (Could you wait a moment?). To offer something: <tur>Çay ister misiniz?</tur> (Would you like some tea?)."
        },
        {
          "t": "ex",
          "items": [
            {
              "tr": "Her sabah erken kalkarım.",
              "fr": "I get up early every morning."
            },
            {
              "tr": "Genellikle otobüsle işe giderim.",
              "fr": "I usually go to work by bus."
            },
            {
              "tr": "Çocukken her yaz köye giderdik.",
              "fr": "As a child, we went to the village every summer."
            },
            {
              "tr": "Bana yardım eder misin?",
              "fr": "Can you help me?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "t": "note",
          "kind": "tip",
          "tag": "Frequency",
          "text": "<tur>her zaman</tur> (always), <tur>genellikle</tur> (usually), <tur>sık sık</tur> (often), <tur>bazen</tur> (sometimes), <tur>nadiren</tur> (rarely), <tur>asla</tur> (never)."
        }
      ],
      "vocab": [
