      "level": "B1",
      "title": "Obligation, necessity and likes",
      "goal": "Express obligation and necessity, and talk about what you like doing.",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "t": "p",
          "text": "To talk about an activity in general, use the <b>verbal noun</b>: <tur>-mek / -mak</tur>, or <tur>-me / -ma</tur> when it carries a case suffix: <tur>yüzmek</tur> (to swim), <tur>yüzmeyi seviyorum</tur> (I like swimming)."
        },
        {
          "t": "table",
          "caption": "Expressing obligation and necessity",
          "head": [
            "Structure",
            "Example",
            "Meaning"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "-meli / -malı",
              "<tur>Gitmeliyim.</tur>",
              "I must leave."
            ],
            [
              "-meliydi / -malıydı",
              "<tur>Gitmeliydim.</tur>",
              "I should have left."
            ],
            [
              "-memeli / -mamalı",
              "<tur>Gitmemelisin.</tur>",
              "You must not leave."
            ],
            [
              "-mek zorunda",
              "<tur>Çalışmak zorundayım.</tur>",
              "I have to work."
            ],
            [
              "-meye ihtiyaç",
              "<tur>Su içmeye ihtiyacım var.</tur>",
              "I need to drink water."
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "t": "note",
          "kind": "info",
          "tag": "Nuance",
          "text": "<b>-meli</b> expresses a personal obligation, advice or a deduction («I must», «I have to»). <b>zorunda</b> stresses an outside constraint. <b>ihtiyaç</b> refers to a need. In the past, <tur>-meliydi</tur> expresses regret about an obligation you did not fulfil: <tur>Daha erken kalkmalıydım.</tur> (I should have got up earlier.)"
        },
        {
          "t": "p",
          "text": "For likes: <tur>sevmek</tur> (to like, to love), <tur>hoşlanmak</tur> (to enjoy), <tur>nefret etmek</tur> (to hate). The activity you like takes <b>-meyi / -mayı</b>: <tur>Yürümeyi seviyorum.</tur>"
        },
        {
          "t": "ex",
          "items": [
